  "text": "(c) THE TOWN ADMINISTRATOR MAY IMPOSE MORE RESTRICTIVE\nDATES AND TIMES FOR HIGH-FREQUENCY USERS TO REDUCE\nCONFLICTS WITH PEAK TRAFFIC PERIODS, PEDESTRIANS, AND SPECIAL\nEVENTS.\nSection 3. Section 10.18.040 is amended by the addition of new subsections (5) and (6)\nto read:\n10.18.040 Exemptions. The following activities are exempt form this Chapter 10.18\n(1)...\n(5) THE TOWN ADMINISTRATOR MAY EXEMPT, ON A CASE-BY-CASE\nBASIS, PUBLIC ROADWAY MAINTENANCE PROJECTS, PRIVATE OR\nQUASI-PUBLIC UTILITY EMERGENCY WORK OR CONCRETE\nCONSTRUCTION ACTIVITIES, FOR OPERATIONAL FLEXIBILITY AS MAY\nBENECESSARY.\n(6) THE TOWN ADMINISTROR, IN CONSULTATION WITH THE CLEAR\nCREEK SHERIFF, IS GRANTED AUTHORITY TO GRANT ONE OR MORE\nEXEMPTIONS FROM THIS CHAPTER 10.18 TO ALLOW TRUCK HAULING\nDURING EXTREME WEATHER EVENTS, EMERGENCIES, OR TRAFFIC\nDIVERSIONS. SUCH EXEMPTIONS MAY BE TO ROUTES, DURATION,\nTIMES OR OTHER CONDITIONS RESPONSIVE TO THE SPECIFIC\nSITUATION.\nSection 4. Section 10.18.050 is amended by the addition of new subsections (g) and (h)\nto read:\n10.18.050 - Permit required; process; reconsideration; appeal; DURATIONS;\nRENEWAL; FEES.\n(a)...\n(g) TRUCK HAUL PERMITS SHALL HAVE A STANDARD DURATION OF 90\nDAYS UNLESS A SPECIFIC DURATION IS IMPOSED BY THE TOWN\nADMINISTRATOR.\n(h) A PERMIT FEE BASED ON THE NUMBER OF AUTHORIZED TRIPS AND\nANTICIPATED ROADWAY IMPACTS SHALL BE PAID AT APPLICATION, AS\nSET FORTH IN THE TOWN'S PERMIT FEE SCHEDULE UNDER CODE\nSECTION 3.16.010.\nSection 5. Section 10.18.060 of the Code is amended to read:\n10.18.060 - Permit conditions.\n(a) The Town Administrator may impose any of the following conditions upon an approved\ntruck haul permit, which conditions may be more stringent than, or in addition to, the\nrestrictions of this Chapter:\n2",
